## Red remediation F-G1 (blocker from Green, HEAD fa8ad4fd3)

Finding: `tutor-commission.settlement.adversarial.test.ts` contradicted spec D-6
inside one file. The helper `settledVariant` returned `zero` for own volume 0
with legs, and line 438 pinned `zero` for own 0 and legs [3], while line 613
pinned `needsOwnStudents` for the same shape. Nine parity failures printed
`variant: module needsOwnStudents settlement zero`.

Fix (commit `b1f1c3cdc`, this file only):

1. `settledVariant` now returns the four D-6 states: `zero` only when the
   network volume is 0; `needsOwnStudents` when the own volume is 0 with legs
   that carry volume; `ownOnly` and `withLegs` as before. The JSDoc names the
   four states and cites spec D-6.
2. Line 438 expects `needsOwnStudents`; its comment says settlement still names
   needsOwnStudents.
3. The random-parity `coverage` object gains the `needsOwnStudents` key, with a
   branch-reach floor above 100, so the sample proves the new branch.

Scan of the whole file: no other case pins the old 3-state rule for that shape
(line 613 already took `needsOwnStudents`; line 617 checks `not.toBe("zero")`,
which both states satisfy).

Verification: `pnpm --filter www-reading-advantage exec vitest run
src/lib/tutor-commission.settlement.adversarial.test.ts --reporter=dot
--silent=true --maxWorkers=1` through heavy-run exits 0, 37 passed (37).
`tsc --noEmit -p .` exits 0. Commit header: the orchestrator message was 102
characters, so the commit uses `test(www): align the settlement variant
(track_id: www_tutor_followups_20261118)`.

